# Separate files/identities are used for admission and preparation.
CONTROL_ENDPOINT=https://127.0.0.1:18443
CONTROL_CLIENT_CERT_FILE=/etc/engineering-platform/tls/REPLACE.crt
CONTROL_CLIENT_KEY_FILE=/etc/engineering-platform/tls/REPLACE.key
CONTROL_SERVER_CA_FILE=/etc/engineering-platform/tls/ca.crt

# Admission and preparation are ALTERNATIVE claimers, not successive stages.
# Canonical admission:   --profile=worker/admission-production --admission-only
# Canonical preparation: --profile=worker/codex-production --prepare-only
# Give each distinct mTLS principal ONLY its matching worker_profiles grant.
# Admission needs worker:poll + worker:report; preparation additionally needs
# worker:prepare. Mixed-capability polling principals on one profile are rejected
# by Core policy loading. Same-kind replicas may share a profile. Never grant
# worker:prepare to an admission-only process to bypass this configuration check.
# Core also denies preparation-capable identities at plain /worker/claim and
# /worker/report, even for their own profile. Preparation uses /prepare-claim
# and /prepared; shared /renew remains subject to the exact identity and lease.
# The server route selects the lane, never a client-supplied mode or local flag.
# Do not rewrite existing RunInput/receipts or requeue a terminal INPUT_VALIDATED
# row to change lanes. Already misrouted work needs explicit reconciliation.
# Do not deploy both modes against one profile or assume admission is followed
# automatically by preparation. Source-bearing Runs select the preparation lane.
# Preparation ONLY also requires an explicit host-owned, owner-private config:
# WORKER_PREPARATION_CONFIG=/etc/engineering-platform/worker-preparation.json
# That config contains per-Run approvals and exact source/Context identities.
# Admission must not receive it, a source root, or Publisher credentials.
